<h2>Four real purchase scenarios that change the math</h2>
<h3>Case 1 — BMW owner needs only supported feature coding</h3><p>Start with the BimmerCode vehicle and coding-option list. If the desired function is documented, the owner can use the US iOS App Store price as one dated example only when that is their actual purchase channel. Add the exact app-approved adapter cost if it is not already owned. BimmerLink's fault-diagnostic license is not automatically required for a coding-only goal. A ProTool coding license might be an alternative for an eligible Android owner, but its exact vehicle and license scope must still be checked. The winner cannot be selected by price alone.</p>
<h3>Case 2 — Reader wants BMW fault data, battery registration and CarPlay</h3><p>BimmerLink documents selected diagnostic and maintenance tasks and offers a separate CarPlay in-app purchase. The buyer should first verify those functions for the car and its installed equipment. The relevant quote includes BimmerLink Full Version, any required adapter and the optional CarPlay add-on only if the extra function will be used. Coding options offered through BimmerCode are not bundled with that license. Someone who already owns a compatible adapter must confirm that its exact model is listed by the developer before assigning a zero equipment cost.</p>
<h3>Case 3 — Workshop owner comparing ProTool Master and BMW AOS</h3><p>ProTool's Master license bundles its documented Android diagnostic and coding functions, but excludes the physical adapter. BMW AOS/TIS provides access to official technical information and ISTA workshop workflows under a distinct regional subscription system. Comparing the ProTool Master license to one day of BMW TIS access as though they serve identical jobs would be misleading. The operator must specify whether the need is an owner-level supported coding operation, fault-guided official diagnostics, repair documentation or programming. Professional software access, approved interfaces and training may dominate license cost.</p>
<h3>Case 4 — Carly for several vehicle brands over three years</h3><p>A brand-specific or multi-brand Carly Premium subscription may be attractive to someone servicing several cars. But public price examples and special bundles are not a guarantee of the user's local checkout terms. Record the exact annual quote and whether the Universal Scanner is included, then model three renewal periods separately from any upfront hardware. Be explicit that future rates and taxes could change. Compare documented feature eligibility on every intended vehicle; a broader license is poor value if the one required BMW function remains unsupported.</p>